    "body": "The independent two-case successor review confirms the bounded C-001/C-002 completion at W10 `808ff934f9cdec7ad8fdc8cdcaa583f1ae068d5e`, preserving the full predecessor review rather than reapproving unrelated owners. The coordinator independently rehashed all5,300 regular files and six symlink entries of the private W02 review,152 native inputs and316 targets; exact Git readback reproduces188 cases/304 occurrences,186 unchanged complete decisions and127 unchanged payloads among128. The original W07 reviewer scopes and individual case/payload review rows remain bound.\n\n- **C-001, case143:** JCM58 supports the nine immediate ISP4 inputs and four nested trace inputs on the authentic named-medium owner. Water input is not a final-yield claim. Hydration, starch grade, commercial premix equivalence and cross-shard trace-owner selection remain unapproved.\n- **C-002, case187:** ingredient1685 explicitly links J209; J209/M98-5 and TOGO M202/JCM209 support the existing carbonate/CO2 stock association. The source does not establish a percentage basis, solvent, carbonate hydrate, CO2 endpoint or stock pH. No duplicate stock is required, and the pure-carbonate alias rejection remains separate.\n\nOne inherited owner correction remains: **W10-SV2-INHERITED-COMPLETENESS-001**, independently also reported as **SCI-CARBONATE-COMPLETENESS-001**. Proposal `sv1-buffers-carbonate_co2_nominal4percent_togo_m202` at `data/ingredients/mapped/carbonate_co2_nominal4percent_togo_m202.yaml` uses `component_assertion.completeness: PARTIAL`. Its complete captured [TOGO M202 source](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M202) names the buffer and100mL receiving dose; it does not establish stock-list closure or explicitly omitted stock constituents. The schema defines PARTIAL as source-explicit omitted constituents and UNKNOWN as unestablished closure. **Use UNKNOWN**, retaining the two label-enumerated parts, all exact sources/history and every preparation unknown; do not add water from another table or infer stock composition. This is the same enum principle documented in1227, extended here to the exact W10 C002 owner rather than assuming that worker-specific tracker already covered it.\n\nThe reviewed stock SHA256 is `e293fdab2a29a678e663d2ca958c2f4babf7bc609ab040bfffd5fbc7232bb68c`. A separate live observation found W10 has advanced to `c9a96da71a1977014680e5a92e600dfc7e3874db`: the stock now hashes to `fa07901e230c7cc707ddacb6f5ff70def989c7d1ecfa40118ef2497136e0e1ce`. That exact delta only corrects the1226 mapping-evidence type and appends history; PARTIAL remains. ISP4 and pure-carbonate rejection payloads, and source decisions21/143/187, remain exact. This bounded observation does not approve the full later successor, which is under a separate independent review.\n\nMake the completeness correction in an immutable successor with truthful appended history, native checks and exact independent re-review. Preserve both original findings and their severity normalization; neither negates the source association. EDTA1225, source-qualified aliases, plant-owner boundaries, W06entry548 nested-trace reconciliation, roles and supported-export holds remain. No whole-owner or release approval is transferred.\n\nCollection: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w10-two-case-review-collection-v1/`. Original private native review YAML SHA256 `6612669c24d9d5eedcc50d92d63a420f3ce80d5736a8add88bc07fb5d849cbbc`; original packet manifest `5ef711c6c1b17b6ac3ddf15d98c580256ef4e12504e1d5701bbae7bf55d70735`. The native pair was validated/rendered privately, not installed by the maintained saver. The exact27 focused controls passed; they do not establish no-clobber publication safety or whole-corpus acceptance. No record, candidate or GitHub object was changed by this collection.\n",
